[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-024-event-driven-architecture-pattern.md#problem-4-difficult-state-synchronization-across-services]

#### Problem 4: Difficult State Synchronization Across Services

**Current State**:

Member demographic changes (address, phone, name) must be synchronized across multiple services:

```csharp
// Member service updates demographic info
public async Task UpdateMemberDemographicsAsync(string memberId, Demographics updates)
{
    // Update member database
    await _memberRepository.UpdateDemographicsAsync(memberId, updates);

    // Synchronously update all dependent services - brittle!
    try { await _claimsClient.UpdateMemberInfoAsync(memberId, updates); }
    catch (Exception ex) { _logger.LogError(\"Failed to sync to claims\"); }

    try { await _portalClient.UpdateMemberInfoAsync(memberId, updates); }
    catch (Exception ex) { _logger.LogError(\"Failed to sync to portal\"); }

    try { await _pharmacyClient.UpdateMemberInfoAsync(memberId, updates); }
    catch (Exception ex) { _logger.LogError(\"Failed to sync to pharmacy\"); }

    // If any sync fails, data inconsistency across services
    // No way to know which services have stale data
}
```

**Impact**:
- **Data Inconsistency**: Member data out of sync across services when updates fail
- **Complex Coordination**: Member service must know about all downstream systems
- **Brittle Integration**: Adding new service requires modifying member service code
- **No Ordering Guarantees**: Updates may arrive out of order creating incorrect final state

