### Real-World Example 2: Member Demographic Synchronization

**Context**: Member address/phone changes must propagate to claims, pharmacy, care management, and portal systems. Synchronous updates caused data inconsistency when any service was down.

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Member service publishes single event
public class MemberService
{
    public async Task UpdateDemographicsAsync(string memberId, Demographics updates)
    {
        // Update member database
        var member = await _repository.UpdateAsync(memberId, updates);

        // Publish event - fire and forget
        await _eventBus.Publish(new MemberUpdatedEvent
        {
            Data = new MemberData
            {
                MemberId = memberId,
                FirstName = member.FirstName,
                LastName = member.LastName,
                Address = member.Address,
                Phone = member.Phone,
                UpdatedFields = updates.ChangedFields
            }
        });
    }
}

// Each consuming service updates independently
public class ClaimsMemberConsumer : IConsumer<MemberUpdatedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<MemberUpdatedEvent> context)
    {
        await _claimsRepository.UpdateMemberInfoAsync(
            context.Message.Data.MemberId,
            context.Message.Data);
    }
}

public class PharmacyMemberConsumer : IConsumer<MemberUpdatedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<MemberUpdatedEvent> context)
    {
        await _pharmacyRepository.UpdateMemberInfoAsync(
            context.Message.Data.MemberId,
            context.Message.Data);
    }
}

// Portal consumer with different data model
public class PortalMemberConsumer : IConsumer<MemberUpdatedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<MemberUpdatedEvent> context)
    {
        // Transform to portal's data model
        var portalMember = _mapper.Map<PortalMember>(context.Message.Data);
        await _portalRepository.UpsertAsync(portalMember);
    }
}
```

**Outcome**:
- **Data Consistency**: Member updates eventually consistent across all systems; no silent failures
- **Service Independence**: Adding new consumer (e.g., care management) doesn't require modifying member service
- **Resilience**: Pharmacy system downtime doesn't prevent member updates; events queue and process on recovery
- **Audit Trail**: Complete history of all member demographic changes in event store for HIPAA compliance

