### Real-World Example 3: Real-Time Fraud Detection Analytics

**Context**: Gainwell Genius analytics needs real-time claim data for fraud detection, but pulling large volumes of claims from the production database impacts performance.

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Analytics service consumes claim events in real-time
public class FraudAnalyticsConsumer : IConsumer<ClaimSubmittedEvent>
{
    private readonly IStreamAnalytics _analytics;

    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<ClaimSubmittedEvent> context)
    {
        var claim = context.Message.Data;

        // Stream to real-time analytics engine
        await _analytics.ProcessClaimAsync(new ClaimAnalyticsEvent
        {
            ClaimId = claim.ClaimId,
            ProviderId = claim.ProviderId,
            ServiceCode = claim.ServiceCode,
            BilledAmount = claim.BilledAmount,
            Timestamp = context.Message.OccurredAt
        });

        // Check for real-time fraud patterns
        var fraudIndicators = await _analytics.DetectPatternsAsync(
            providerId: claim.ProviderId,
            lookbackWindow: TimeSpan.FromHours(24));

        if (fraudIndicators.Any(i => i.Severity == "Critical"))
        {
            await context.Publish(new FraudAlertEvent
            {
                ProviderId = claim.ProviderId,
                Indicators = fraudIndicators,
                RequiresReview = true
            });
        }
    }
}

// Dashboard shows real-time metrics
public class AnalyticsDashboard
{
    // Streaming query over event window
    public async Task<DashboardMetrics> GetRealtimeMetricsAsync()
    {
        return new DashboardMetrics
        {
            ClaimsLast1Hour = await _analytics.CountEventsAsync(
                eventType: "ClaimSubmitted",
                window: TimeSpan.FromHours(1)),

            AverageBilledAmount = await _analytics.AverageAsync(
                eventType: "ClaimSubmitted",
                field: "Data.BilledAmount",
                window: TimeSpan.FromHours(1)),

            TopProviders = await _analytics.TopNAsync(
                eventType: "ClaimSubmitted",
                groupBy: "Data.ProviderId",
                n: 10,
                window: TimeSpan.FromHours(24))
        };
    }
}
```

**Outcome**:
- **Real-Time Detection**: Fraud patterns detected within seconds instead of daily batch processing
- **No Database Impact**: Analytics reads from event stream instead of production database queries
- **Scalable Ingestion**: Kafka handles high-volume event ingestion for analytics without backpressure
